(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Systemic treatment options for moderate plaque psoriasis continue to expand,) Tj
T*
(yet comparative effectiveness data guide clinical decision-making. Methods: This 52-week,) Tj
T*
(phase IV, randomized, open-label comparative effectiveness trial will evaluate two) Tj
T*
(distinct systemic approaches in patients with moderate chronic plaque psoriasis.) Tj
T*
(Approximately 360 adults \(aged >=18 years\) with >=6 months psoriasis duration and candidacy) Tj
T*
(for systemic therapy will be enrolled. Participants will be randomized 1:2 to receive) Tj
T*
(either subcutaneous injections of an IL-23-pathway inhibitor or daily oral) Tj
T*
(phosphodiesterase-4 inhibitor. Primary outcomes at 16 weeks will be achievement of >=90%) Tj
T*
(skin clearance and physician-rated complete or nearly-complete clearing with >=2-grade) Tj
T*
(improvement. At 16 weeks, those receiving the oral agent will be re-randomized based on) Tj
T*
(treatment response, allowing comparison of switching strategies. Secondary outcomes) Tj
T*
(include sustained response at 52 weeks, safety/adverse event profiles, treatment) Tj
T*
(satisfaction, and quality-of-life measures. This pragmatic comparative effectiveness) Tj
T*
(design will provide real-world efficacy and safety data to inform treatment selection.) Tj
